Functions Expressions enable JavaScript a very powerful programming language.
Function Expressions are NOT hoisted
The following are types of function expressions
Anonymous : These are nammeless functions which are not given any identifier 
        


IIFE - Immediately Invoked Functions Expressions : These allowed a function to be executed immediately.
        You do not want the variables declared inside the functions to be part of the Global Environment.
        {
                let message = "Hello, World";
                function displayMessage(){
                console.log(message);
                }
                displayMessage();
        }()
        //This could have be an anonymous function but it has been 
        //invoked immediately.
        
        This will be away from your Global Scope Context
        This is a very good example of Encapsulation
        This also promotes some sort of privacy
        The variable inside them cannot be access outside the function 
        scope
